  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "About three hundred years before news of the Three Kings inheritance spreads through Southern Border, Wu clan exterminates Wang clan, its mortal enemy, absorbing its remnant forces and rising into a large clan that owns three mountains. The attack misses three children: an eight year old boy who becomes King Quan, a five year old boy who becomes King Bao, and a six year old girl who becomes King Xin. Wu clan sends a lazy assassin to finish them, and he fakes their deaths rather than complete the task, unintentionally sparing them.",
      "chapters": [
        324
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_three_kings_inheritance",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "fac_wu_clan",
        "char_king_quan",
        "char_king_bao",
        "char_king_xin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The three survive on their own, grow close through hardship, and are eventually thrown into an ancient inheritance ground left by a rank six Gu Immortal, where each inherits a portion of the legacy and cultivates for nearly a hundred years until all three reach rank five. They then return and wipe out Wu clan in three days: King Quan’s hound army engulfs Wu clan’s village, King Xin kills the higher-ups and leaves them leaderless, and King Bao’s violent attacks shatter the mountain rock.",
      "chapters": [
        324
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After their revenge, the three kings choose not to rebuild Wang clan, reasoning that a clan, however strong, could not defend against true experts, and instead live in seclusion until their inheritance ground reopens generations later.",
      "chapters": [
        324
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
